# Copy to $GNEWS_LAB_DIR/exits.tsv and edit. Label, TAB, gluetun selection.
#
# The label names the row in results/, so keep it stable: comparing an address across days is
# the point. The selection is passed to gluetun verbatim, so anything it accepts works --
# SERVER_HOSTNAMES pins one server, SERVER_COUNTRIES lets it choose within a country.
#
# Pin a hostname when you want the same exit twice; a country will wander between runs, and the
# throttle is per address, so a wandering exit quietly changes the thing being measured. The
# address is recorded in every row either way, so you can always tell after the fact.
#
# List what is available:
#   docker run --rm --entrypoint /gluetun-entrypoint qmcgaw/gluetun format-servers -protonvpn
#
# Nine exits were in use before this harness moved to gluetun. Eight survive; Nicaragua is
# absent from gluetun's bundled Proton list, so NI-1 has no equivalent here.
dominican-republic	SERVER_HOSTNAMES=node-do-01.protonvpn.net
ecuador	SERVER_HOSTNAMES=node-ec-01.protonvpn.net
israel	SERVER_HOSTNAMES=node-il-04.protonvpn.net
korea	SERVER_HOSTNAMES=node-kr-03.protonvpn.net
latvia	SERVER_HOSTNAMES=node-lv-01.protonvpn.net
norway	SERVER_HOSTNAMES=node-no-05.protonvpn.net
tanzania	SERVER_HOSTNAMES=tz-03.protonvpn.net
united-states	SERVER_HOSTNAMES=node-us-119.protonvpn.net
